From 74b9347149f2139e9ea16a5309c9a2fd656db121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a parked run's own checkpoint note does not
 re-arm active_pr

An owner that parks orderly (scheduled/continued) and then writes its checkpoint note
restating its PR a few seconds later was held on its wake: the guard read its own note as
publication newer than the park (MacBook t_01a1cff0541bf30c, park 06:48:32 PST, own note
06:48:39 naming PR #1486, held until an operator `kanban resume`).

The note now belongs to the park when its commented event names exactly the parking run
(portable writer_run_uid on synced schemas, the local integer only on unsynced ones, one
event per row), it precedes any later claim, and every PR it names was already named in this
card's own PR comments before the park. Other runs' notes, chats, new PRs and unreadable
provenance keep today's hold. test_kanban_pickup_event_history's park+repeat case now covers
both: restating the parked PR resumes (hub and picked-up replica), a new PR still holds.

Proof:
- RED on the base: the 4 repro cases (scheduled/continued x local/synced) returned
  active_pr; GREEN after.
- Replay over copies of every hub kanban DB and sync-shadow (2,089 evaluations at now and
  park+600 s, 7 days): 2 changed, both this class. The incident cut at 15:04:45Z goes
  active_pr -> None; t_01a1af251a1c7525 (run 25830 continued 05:43:17, same-uid note at
  05:43:38 restating daveey/hermes#907) goes active_pr -> None.
- Mutants: 21 run, 19 killed. 2 survivors are equivalent: an unreadable park time read as
  epoch 0 leaves the known-PR set empty, and re-timing pre-park comments to park-1 keeps
  them before the park.

Card: t_01a1d04fee42c1c7
